# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/gitoid node411
node411 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>gitoid</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/gitoid' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/gitoid</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Gitoid &lt;https://www.iana.org/assignments/uri-schemes/prov/gitoid&gt;, stands for Git Object ID &lt;https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-Objects&gt;. A gitoid of type blob is a unique hash of a binary artifact. A gitoid may represent either an Artifact Identifier &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-identifier-types&gt; for the software artifact or an Input Manifest Identifier &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#input-manifest-identifier&gt; for the software artifact&#x27;s associated Artifact Input Manifest &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-input-manifest&gt;; this ambiguity exists because the Artifact Input Manifest is itself an artifact, and the gitoid of that artifact is its valid identifier. Gitoids calculated on software artifacts (Snippet, File, or Package Elements) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 SoftwareArtifact&#x27;s contentIdentifier property. Gitoids calculated on the Artifact Input Manifest (Input Manifest Identifier) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 Element&#x27;s externalIdentifier property. See OmniBOR Specification &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/&gt;, a minimalistic specification for describing software Artifact Dependency Graphs &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-dependency-graph-adg&gt;.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Gitoid &lt;https://www.iana.org/assignments/uri-schemes/prov/gitoid&gt;, stands for Git Object ID &lt;https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-Objects&gt;. A gitoid of type blob is a unique hash of a binary artifact. A gitoid may represent either an Artifact Identifier &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-identifier-types&gt; for the software artifact or an Input Manifest Identifier &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#input-manifest-identifier&gt; for the software artifact&#x27;s associated Artifact Input Manifest &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-input-manifest&gt;; this ambiguity exists because the Artifact Input Manifest is itself an artifact, and the gitoid of that artifact is its valid identifier. Gitoids calculated on software artifacts (Snippet, File, or Package Elements) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 SoftwareArtifact&#x27;s contentIdentifier property. Gitoids calculated on the Artifact Input Manifest (Input Manifest Identifier) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 Element&#x27;s externalIdentifier property. See OmniBOR Specification &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/&gt;, a minimalistic specification for describing software Artifact Dependency Graphs &lt;https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-dependency-graph-adg&gt;.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/ExpandedLicensing/OrLaterOperator node412
node412 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>OrLaterOperator</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/ExpandedLicensing/OrLaterOperator' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/ExpandedLicensing/OrLaterOperator</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Portion of an AnyLicenseInfo representing this version, or any later version,
of the indicated License.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Portion of an AnyLicenseInfo representing this version, or any later version,
of the indicated License.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;An OrLaterOperator indicates that this portion of the AnyLicenseInfo
represents either (1) the specified version of the corresponding License, or
(2) any later version of that License. It is represented in the SPDX License
Expression Syntax by the + operator.

It is context-dependent, and unspecified by SPDX, as to what constitutes a
&quot;later version&quot; of any particular License. Some Licenses may not be versioned,
or may not have clearly-defined ordering for versions. The consumer of SPDX
data will need to determine for themselves what meaning to attribute to a
&quot;later version&quot; operator for a particular License.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/UseAction node413
node413 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>UseAction</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/UseAction' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/UseAction</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The action of product use.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The action of product use.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;This is the specific action of product use.

Relationship:

For each UseAction there is at least one /Core/Relationship class or subclass with the relationshipType of &#x27;performedBy’ on the from and a /Core/Agent class or subclass on the to.

For each UseAction there is at least one /Core/Relationship class or subclass with the relationshipType of &#x27;affects’ on the from and a /Core/Element class or subclass on the to.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
